  "title": "74: al-Muddassir المدثر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُۙ‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL AL-MUDDASSERU.\nO’ thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) covered under thy mantle!\nقُمْ فَاَنْذِرْۙ‏(2)\nQUM FAANZER.\nArise (thou) and warn (mankind)!\nوَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْۙ‏(3)\nWA RABBAKA FAKABBER.\nAnd thy Lord, magnify!\nوَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرْۙ‏(4)\nWASEEABAKA FATAHHER.\nAnd thy raiment, purify!\nوَالرُّجْزَ فَاهْجُرْۙ‏(5)\nWAALRRUJZA FAAHJUR.\nAnd every kind of abomination, Shun it!\nوَلَا تَمْنُنْ تَسْتَكْثِرُۙ‏(6)\nWA LAA TAMNUN TASTAKSERU.\nAnd bestow not favours (expecting) that thou mayest receive them back increased\nوَ لِرَبِّكَ فَاصْبِرْؕ‏(7)\nWA LE-RABBEKA FAASBER.\nAnd for (the sake of) thy Lord (endure every hardship) in patience!\nفَاِذَا نُقِرَ فِى النَّاقُوْرِۙ‏(8)\nFA-EZAA NUQERA FIL AN-NAAQOORE.\nFor when the Trumpet is beaten\nفَذٰلِكَ يَوْمَئِذٍ يَّوْمٌ عَسِيْرٌۙ‏(9)\nFA-ZAALEKAL YAWMA-EZIN YYAWMUN A’ASEERUN.\nThat, that shall be the Day of distress (for those who disbelieve)\nعَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ غَيْرُ يَسِيْرٍ‏(10)\nA’LAL KAAFEREEN GHAYRO YASEERIN.\nUnto the disbelievers (it shall be) anything other than ease!\nذَرْنِىْ وَمَنْ خَلَقْتُ وَحِيْدًا ۙ‏(11)\nZARNEAA WA MAN KHALAQTU WAHEEDAN.\nLeave Me (to deal with) him whom I created (bare and) alone!\nوَّجَعَلْتُ لَهٗ مَالًا مَّمْدُوْدًا ۙ‏(12)\nWWAJAA’ALTU LAHU MAALAWN MMAMDOODAN.\nAnd unto whom I granted wealth in abundance!\nوَّبَنِيْنَ شُهُوْدًا ۙ‏(13)\nWWABANEENA SHUHOODAN.\nAnd sons abiding in his presence!\nوَّمَهَّدتُّ لَهٗ تَمْهِيْدًا ۙ‏(14)\nWWAMAHHADTTU LAHU TAMHEEDAN.\nAnd unto whom I made (life) adjustably smooth!\nثُمَّ يَطْمَعُ اَنْ اَزِيْدَ  ۙ‏(15)\nSUMMA YATMAU’U AN AAZEEDA.\nAnd yet desireth he that I should further add!\nكَلَّا ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ لِاٰيٰتِنَا عَنِيْدًا ؕ‏(16)\nKALLAA INNAHU KAANA LE-AAYAATENAA A’ANEEDAN.\nNever (it shall be)! for unto Our signs he was a foe!\nسَاُرْهِقُهٗ صَعُوْدًا ؕ‏(17)\nSAARHEQUH SAU’OODAN.\nSoon will I make him afflicted of a severe punishment\nاِنَّهٗ فَكَّرَ وَقَدَّرَۙ‏(18)\nINNAHU FAKKARA WA QADDARA.\nVerily, he thought and determined\nفَقُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَۙ‏(19)\nFA QOTELAL KAYFA QADDARA.\nBut may he be ruined how he determined\nثُمَّ قُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَۙ‏(20)\nSUMMA QOTELAL KAYFA QADDARA.\nAgain may be he ruined how he determined!\nثُمَّ نَظَرَۙ‏(21)\nSUMMA NAZARA.\nThen looked he around!\nثُمَّ عَبَسَ وَبَسَرَۙ‏(22)\nSUMMA A’BASA WABASARA.\nThen frowned he and scowled!\nثُمَّ اَدْبَرَ وَاسْتَكْبَرَۙ‏(23)\nSUMMA AADBARA WAS TAKBAR.\nThen turned he his back and swelled in pride!\nفَقَالَ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ يُّؤْثَرُۙ‏(24)\nFAQAALA IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM YYUSARU.\nThen said he: “This is naught but sorcery from of old!\nاِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا قَوْلُ الْبَشَرِؕ‏(25)\nIN HAAZAA ILLAA QAWLU AL-BASHARE.\nThis is naught but the word of a human being!\nسَاُصْلِيْهِ سَقَرَ‏(26)\nSAASLEEHE SAQARA.\nSoon will I cast him into hell!\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا سَقَرُؕ‏(27)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA SAQARU.\nAnd what will make him realize what hell is?\nلَا تُبْقِىْ وَ لَا تَذَرُۚ‏(28)\nLAA TUBQEAA WA LAA TAZARU.\nIt leaveth not nor it spareth (aught)\nلَوَّاحَةٌ لِّلْبَشَرِۖۚ‏(29)\nLAWAHATUN LLELBASHARE.\nIt shrivelleth a human body!\nعَلَيْهَا تِسْعَةَ عَشَرَؕ‏(30)\nA’LAYHAA TESA’ATA A’ASHARA.\nAbove it (guardians) are nineteen!\nوَمَا جَعَلْنَاۤ اَصْحٰبَ النَّارِ اِلَّا مَلٰٓئِكَةً وَّمَا جَعَلْنَا عِدَّتَهُمْ اِلَّا فِتْنَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ۙ لِيَسْتَيْقِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ وَيَزْدَادَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِيْمَانًا وَّلَا يَرْتَابَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ وَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ وَلِيَقُوْلَ الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ وَّالْكٰفِرُوْنَ مَاذَاۤ اَرَادَ اللّٰهُ بِهٰذَا مَثَلًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُوْدَ رَبِّكَ اِلَّا هُوَ ؕ وَمَا هِىَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٰى لِلْبَشَرِ‏(31)\nWA MAA JA-A’LNAA MASALAN NAAR ILLAA MALAAA-EKATAN WA MAA JA-A’LNAA E’EDDATAHUM ILLAA FETNATAN LIL-LAZEENA KAFAROO LEESTAYQENA LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA WAYAZDAADA LAZEENA AAMANOO EEMAANAW WA LAA YARTAABA LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA WAL MO’MENOONA WALEEQOOLA LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN WWAALKAAFEROONA MAA ARAADA LAAHO BEHAAZAA MASALAA KAZAALEKA YOZILLO LAAHO MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE MAN YASHAAA-O WA MAA YA’LAMO JUNOODA RABBEKA ILLAA HOWA WA MAA HEYA ILLAA ZEKRAA LIL-BASHARE.\nWe have made not the guardians of the fire other than angels, and We have made not the number save as a trial for those who disbelieve, that certain may be those who have been given the book, and may increase those who believe in (their) faith, and may doubt not those who have been given the book and the believers, and that say those in whose hearts is a distress and the disbelievers: “What meaneth God by this similitude?” Thus doth God alloweth to stray whomsoever He willeth, and guideth He whom He willeth, And knoweth not (any one) the hosts of God save He Himself; And this is naught but a reminder unto mankind\nكَلَّا وَالْقَمَرِۙ‏(32)\nKALLAA WAL QAMARE.\nNay! By the moon!\nوَالَّيْلِ اِذْ اَدْبَرَۙ‏(33)\nWAL LAYLE IZ AADBARA.\nAnd by the night when it retreateth!\nوَالصُّبْحِ اِذَاۤ اَسْفَرَۙ‏(34)\nWAS SUBHE EZAA AASFARA.\nAnd by the morn when it brighteneth!\nاِنَّهَا لَاِحْدَى الْكُبَرِۙ‏(35)\nINNAHAA LAAHDAA AL-KUBARE.\nVerily it (the Hell) is one of the grievous woes!\nنَذِيْرًا لِّلْبَشَرِۙ‏(36)\nNAZEERAN LLELBASHARE.\nA warning (it is) unto mankind!\nلِمَنْ شَآءَ مِنْكُمْ اَنْ يَّتَقَدَّمَ اَوْ يَتَاَخَّرَؕ‏(37)\nLEMAN-Y SHAAA-AL MINKUM AN YYATAQADDAMA AW YATAAKKHARA.\nUnto him among you who desireth to go forward (in goodness) or to remain behind\nكُلُّ نَفْسٍ ۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ رَهِيْنَةٌ ۙ‏(38)\nKULLO NAFSIM BEMAA KASABAT RAHEENATUN.\nEvery soul, for what it earned, is held in pledge!\nاِلَّاۤ اَصْحٰبَ الْيَمِيْنِۛ ؕ‏(39)\nILLAA MASALAN YAMEENE.\nSave the people of the Right hand\nفِىْ جَنّٰتٍ ۛ يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَۙ‏(40)\nFEE JANNAATIN YATASAAA-ALOON.\nIn gardens shall they be, asking each other\nعَنِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(41)\nA’NIL MUJREMEEN.\nAbout the guilty ones\nمَا سَلَكَكُمْ فِىْ سَقَرَ‏(42)\nMAA SALAKAKUM FEE SAQARA.\nWhat hath brought you into the hell!\nقَالُوْا لَمْ نَكُ مِنَ الْمُصَلِّيْنَۙ‏(43)\nQAALOO LAM NAKU MENAL AL-MUSALLEENA.\nThey shall say: “We were not of those who offered the regular prayers (to God)\nوَلَمْ نَكُ نُطْعِمُ الْمِسْكِيْنَۙ‏(44)\nWA LAM NAKU NUTE’EMU MISKEENA.\nAnd we used not to feed the poor!\nوَكُنَّا نَخُوْضُ مَعَ الْخَآئِضِيْنَۙ‏(45)\nKUNNAA NAKHOOZU LAAHA AL-KHAAEZEENA.\nAnd used we to talk vanities with the vain talkers!\nوَ كُنَّا نُكَذِّبُ بِيَوْمِ الدِّيْنِۙ‏(46)\nWA KUNNAA NUKAZZEBU BE-YAWMID DEENE.\nAnd used we to belie the Day of Judgment!\nحَتّٰٓى اَتٰٮنَا الْيَقِيْنُؕ‏(47)\nHATTAA AATAANAA AL-YAQEENU.\nTill came upon us the Certainty (death)\nفَمَا تَنْفَعُهُمْ شَفَاعَةُ الشّٰفِعِيْنَؕ‏(48)\nFAMAA TANFAU’UHUM SHAFAAA’ATU ASH-SHAAFEE’EENA.\nSo, shall avail them not the intercession of the intercessors!\nفَمَا لَهُمْ عَنِ التَّذْكِرَةِ مُعْرِضِيْنَۙ‏(49)\nFAMAA LAHUM A’NIL AT-TAZKERATE MOA’REZEEN.\nWhat hath happened then (unto them) that they turn aside from the warning\nكَاَنَّهُمْ حُمُرٌ مُّسْتَنْفِرَةٌ ۙ‏(50)\nKA-ANNAHUM HUMURUN MMUSTANFERATUN.\nAs if they were asses affrighted\nفَرَّتْ مِنْ قَسْوَرَةٍ ؕ‏(51)\nFARRAT MIN QASWARATIN.\nFleeing from a lion\nبَلْ يُرِيْدُ كُلُّ امْرِىٴٍ مِّنْهُمْ اَنْ يُّؤْتٰى صُحُفًا مُّنَشَّرَةً ۙ‏(52)\nBAL YOREEDO KULLO AMREAA MINHUM AN YYUTAA SOHOFAM MMUNASSHARATAN.\nNay! But willeth every one of them that he may be given (the heavenly book) in open pages spread out\nكَلَّا ؕ بَلْ لَّا يَخَافُوْنَ الْاٰخِرَةَ ؕ‏(53)\nKALLAA BAL LAA YAKHAAFOONA AAKHERATA.\nNay! But they fear not the hereafter!\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّهٗ تَذْكِرَةٌ ۚ‏(54)\nKALLAA INNAHU TAZKERAH.\nNay! Verily it is a Reminder!\nفَمَنْ شَآءَ ذَكَرَهٗ ؕ‏(55)\nFAMAN SHAAA-AL ZAKARAH.\nSo whosoever willeth may mind it\nوَمَا يَذْكُرُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُ ؕ هُوَ اَهْلُ التَّقْوٰى وَاَهْلُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ‏(56)\nWA MAA YAZKUROONA ILLAA AN YASHAAA-AL LAAHO HOWA AAHLU TAQWAA WAAHLU AL-MAGHFERATE.\nThey will mind it not unless God willeth; Worthy is He to be feared. And worthy is He to seek refuge to",
  "merits": "Surah al-Muddassir (The Clothed One)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 56 verses. Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) has said that the person who recites this Surah in his compulsory prayers will attain a rank near the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) in the hereafter and will be protected from any misfortunes in this world.\nIf this Surah is recited daily and then a dua is made after its recitation, then the dua will be answered and the need will be fulfilled. If one makes dua that he wishes to memorize the whole Qur’an then he will not die until he has memorized it."
